# Unapplied CYD static RX reserve candidate

This additive archive records a host/config proof and an isolated actual SDK
ten-variant target campaign. The exact completed target report SHA is
`@@TARGET_SHA@@`. The corrected candidate module SHA is
`77db50af0ff65dfa333b28584b48632c625d999984e7ff8fffd48cb0e52cdb0f`.
The candidate has not been integrated into production or the radio audio owner.

Evidence includes four strict ASan/UBSan host groups, six named semantic controls,
the original public-getter const compile rejection,14 invalid host configs and
24 real configure-only projects. Later target preparation adds a17-source SDK
guard closure with22 offline guard checks. Different historical helper/source
versions remain distinct; earlier host/config coverage is not relabelled as
identical-byte coverage of the later helper.

The isolated target campaign uses pinned SDK6.0.2, Xtensa ELF machine94, real
SDK headers and allocator function-pointer routes. Its ten outcomes include six
exact semantic detections and four independent real reserve/reclaim on/off
builds. Positive runs distinguish injected setup rollback from actual heap
pressure and canonical reclaim recovery. Two-core ownership/erase handover,
ordinary unrelated allocation/free and reserve-off public setup/reset/free
paths are observed only within that fixture. The SDK-derived capacity is kept
as observed; no guessed fixed storage number or physical memory saving is
claimed. RX content stays16384 and TX content4096; dynamic/variable RX is excluded.

Raw reports, source/config snapshots, generated spans, recipes, full compiler
and runtime logs, compiled-header closure, ELF/data-word metadata and all
hash relationships are preserved without rewriting their bytes. Long paths
flatten into content-addressed objects; large text uses deterministic gzip.
Whole ELFs, host/target binaries, flash images, objects, libraries, ROMs and tool
executables are explicit hash/size/role omissions. Linux tool hashes are the
original host's recorded observations, not new packaging observations.

Run `python -B verify.py` for a standalone offline manifest, raw/gzip identity,
JSON-binding and selected-entry/oracle check. It reads only this directory.
Omitted binaries remain necessary to independently repeat a full binary
inspection. Historical failures and unbuilt preparation reports keep their
original scope; they are not rewritten into successful target reports.

Production integration, audio-owner lifetime/cancellation, canonical lint and
application firmware qualification remain pending. Physical TLS/full-record,
protocol conformance, resource/fragmentation/usefulness and default activation
are unproven. No network, device or crypto operation is performed by packaging.
AAC, Ogg and deferred FLAC work are excluded.
